SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"UK court papers reveal PTI donor bought three properties on behalf of Shehbaz Sharif","publisher":"Geo News","publication_date":"2022-02-10","url":"https://www.geo.tv/amp/398231-pti-donor-bought-property-on-behalf-of-shehbaz-sharif","claim":"Court papers from the NCA investigation say Aneel Mussarat bought a London property on behalf of Shehbaz Sharif and helped buy two others, and that Sharif's lawyers told the NCA the purchases were made on his behalf.","locator":"paragraphs 2-4, lines 29-36","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Secondary reporting, but it quotes court papers and Sharif's lawyers with concrete transaction details.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Published in 2022 and directly relevant to the 2022 integrity review, although the underlying transactions predate 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Directly tied to Sharif through his lawyers' account and the NCA file; it shows private property dealings, not proof of office-derived self-dealing in 2022.","contrary_evidence":["The same report says the loans were repaid on time and that the NCA later failed to find a link between Sharif's assets and criminal origin or misuse of public office."],"lenses":["7B.3","7B.4","7B.6","7B.7"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"PM Shehbaz Sharif has overseas assets worth Rs130 million: ECP","publisher":"ARY News","publication_date":"2022-06-15","url":"https://arynews.tv/pm-shehbaz-sharif-has-overseas-assets-worth-rs130-million-ecp","claim":"ECP data released in June 2022 reported that Shehbaz Sharif had about Rs245 million in assets, Rs130.74 million in overseas assets, Rs20 million in bank accounts, and a Rs60 million loan from his son Salman Sharif.","locator":"lines 52-57","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"It reproduces the ECP's released wealth data, but the article itself is still a media report rather than the primary filing.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Published in 2022 using the ECP's FY2021 assets release, which sits squarely inside the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Sharif's own asset declaration; it indicates family-linked liabilities and overseas holdings but does not by itself prove illicit enrichment from office.","contrary_evidence":["The report also says his assets fell by 3 percent and does not itself allege misuse of office."],"lenses":["7B.3","7B.4","7B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Transcript of the Press Briefing by Spokesperson on Monday, 25 April, 2022","publisher":"Ministry of Foreign Affairs, Government of Pakistan","publication_date":"2022-04-25","url":"https://mofa.gov.pk/transcript-of-the-press-briefing-by-spokesperson-on-monday-25-april-2022","claim":"The ministry transcript says the National Security Committee examined the cypher matter, found no evidence of any conspiracy, and stated there was no question or possibility of hiding or holding back the document.","locator":"lines 151-154, 159, and 172-174","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official government transcript with direct contemporaneous account of the committee's conclusion and the spokesperson's answers.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Fully within 2022 and directly tied to the foreign-conspiracy claim that dominated the early Sharif period.","ruler_attribution":"This reflects the government's handling under Sharif's new administration and chairmanship of the NSC; it is good evidence of willingness to submit the claim to official scrutiny, not independent forensic proof of all facts.","contrary_evidence":["It is an official account of the government's conclusion, so it does not independently verify the underlying cable or resolve all competing political narratives."],"lenses":["7B.2","7B.6","7B.8"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"New Pak PM Says Will Step Down If Foreign Conspiracy Claim Proved","publisher":"NDTV","publication_date":"2022-04-11","url":"https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/new-pakistan-pm-shehbaz-sharif-says-will-step-down-if-imran-khans-foreign-conspiracy-claim-proved-2879523","claim":"In his inaugural speech, Shehbaz Sharif announced a parliamentary probe into the foreign-conspiracy claim and said he would resign if any shred of evidence proved the allegation.","locator":"lines 95-99","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium","source_confidence_reason":"Syndicated reporting of a live speech, with a clear attributed quote but no direct transcript attachment from the outlet itself.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 target period and contemporaneous with the political transition.","ruler_attribution":"Direct statement by Sharif; it shows an explicit commitment to scrutiny and conditional accountability, but not a later correction by him.","contrary_evidence":["A promise to resign if proved is not the same as a later retraction, and it does not by itself establish prior deception or correction."],"lenses":["7B.2","7B.6","7B.8"]}

**Search and Rejection Summary**
I checked the official MOFA transcript, the official PID/National Assembly speech page, ECP asset-release reproductions, Dawn, Geo, ARY, Business Recorder, NDTV, The News, Express Tribune, Gulf News, Pakistan Today, and Daily Mail coverage of the apology.

I retained only items that added something material to the two gaps:
- Personal benefit or hidden-interest nexus: the Geo court-papers item and the ECP asset-release reproductions.
- Truthfulness or correction: the MOFA NSC transcript and the inaugural-speech report from NDTV.
- I reused the 2022 Daily Mail apology and the 2022 benami-account acquittal material already in the index because they are directly relevant and not worth duplicating.

I removed or deprioritized:
- Duplicate summaries of the same ECP asset release.
- Generic commentary, opinion, and reader-response pages.
- Post-2022 follow-up material that did not add anything to the 2022 record.
- Weakly attributable corruption context that did not add a Sharif-specific personal nexus.

Blocker noted:
- The direct ECP asset-table page was not cleanly retrievable in-browser, so I used contemporaneous reporting that reproduced the released ECP data.

**Remaining Gaps**
- Personal-benefit/conflict gap: partly resolved. The record now has a 2022 asset declaration and a 2022 court-paper account of property purchases on Sharif's behalf, but I still do not have the raw ECP filing or NCA bundle itself.
- Truthfulness/correction gap: partly resolved. The record now shows a public commitment to scrutiny and an official NSC conclusion rejecting the conspiracy claim, but I still do not have a clean 2022 instance where Sharif publicly retracts one of his own false statements.
- More search would help if you want a tighter integrity finding on either point, especially if you want primary court-file exhibits or a direct verified transcript of a corrected Sharif statement.
